{Grünfeld Defense: Russian Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. d4 Bg7 5. Qb3 dxc4 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Qxc4 O-O 7. Bf4 c6 8. e4 ! b5 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... c5 Rb1 cxd4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qb3 Bg4 10. e5 Nh5 11. Be3 Bxf3 ?! 12. gxf3 e6 13. Ne4 Nd7 14. O-O-O a5 15. Nd6 Nb6 16. Qc2 Qh4 17. Kb1 Nd5 18. Qxc6 a4 19. Bxb5 a3 20. b3 Nhf4 21. Qc5 Rab8 22. Rd2 Qh3 23. Bc6 f6 24. Bxf4 Nxf4 25. exf6 Bxf6 26. Nc4 Rfc8 27. Qd6 Qh4 28. Rhd1 Be7 29. Qe5 Rd8 30. Qe4 Kg7 31. Rc2 Kg8 32. Ne5 Bd6 33. Nd7 Rb4 34. Qe1 Qxh2 35. Nc5 Rb6 36. Qa5 Bxc5 37. Qxc5 Rbb8 38. Qxa3 Qh4 39. Be4 Qf6 40. Qc1 h5 41. Rc7 h4 42. Rg1 g5 43. Qc5 Rd5 44. Bxd5 Nxd5 45. Rd7 Rd8 46. Rxd8+ Qxd8 47. Qc1 Kf7 48. Qxg5 Qxg5 49. Rxg5 Nf4 50. Rg4 Ng6 51. a4 h3 52. Rg1 Nf4 53. a5 Nd5 54. a6 e5 55. Rh1 Nc3+ 56. Kc2 Nb5 57. Rxh3 Ke6 58. Rh6+ Kf5 59. Kd3 Nc7 60. a7 Na8 61. Rh5+ Kg6 62. Rxe5 Kf7 63. Ke2 Nc7 64. Rc5 Ne6 65. Rc4 Nf4+ 66. Kf1 Ne6 67. a8=Q Kg7 68. Qa6 Kf7 69. d5 Ng7 70. Rc7+ Kg8 71. Qg6 Kf8 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} 72. Qf7# 1-0
